Package: ARGflanker
Title: Prediction of Mobile Genetic Element Linkage to Antibiotic
    Resistance Genes from Short-Read Metagenomes
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Firstname",
           family = "Lastname",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "700049478@uaeu.ac.ae",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0000-0000-0000"))
Description: ARGflanker screens metagenomic gene predictions for antibiotic
    resistance genes (ARGs) that are likely to be mobile, by examining the
    genes that flank them. Rather than relying on a single contig physically
    joining an ARG to a mobile genetic element (MGE) marker (integrase,
    transposase, recombinase, insertion sequence or plasmid replication
    gene), which short-read assembly frequently breaks, it combines three
    lines of evidence: co-location on the same contig within a distance
    window, a data-derived neighbourhood signature of the gene categories
    that typically surround ARGs, and read-pair bridging that links an ARG
    to an MGE marker even when the two sit on separate contigs. The output
    is a per-ARG mobility score with its supporting evidence, intended as a
    hypothesis-generating screen rather than proof of mobility.
